cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Ternary Operating Point: Threshold Control and Annealing in
  1.58-Bit Language Models
message: If you use this artefact, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kilic
    given-names: Haydar
    email: haydar.kilic@ostimteknik.edu.tr
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2551-3772
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Artificial Intelligence Engineering,
      Ostim Technical University, Ankara, Türkiye
repository-code: https://github.com/HAYDARKILIC/tai
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ternary quantization
  - quantization-aware training
  - 1.58-bit language models
  - weight initialization
  - sparsity control
  - threshold annealing
  - pre-registered experimental design
abstract: >-
  Research artefact for a pre-registered study of the ternary operating point
  in 1.58-bit language models: 3,016 persisted runs over an eleven-point scale
  ladder and two architecture families, with the provenance manifest and the
  analysis and figure pipeline. Every table and figure in the paper regenerates
  from the run store without a GPU.
